From: =?utf-8?b?T25kxZllaiBTdXLDvQ==?= <ondrej@sury.org>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:30:00 +0100
Subject: Skip the bug40576 test with the system libxmlrpc-epi

The system libxmlrpc-epi formats doubles with "%f", so xmlrpc_encode()
keeps only six decimal places. The bundled library got the fix for PHP
bug #40576 (upstream commit 8b9bf1e2c3e), the system one did not.
---
 ext/xmlrpc/tests/bug40576_64bit.phpt | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/ext/xmlrpc/tests/bug40576_64bit.phpt b/ext/xmlrpc/tests/bug40576_64bit.phpt
index 926980d..c7c04b0 100644
--- a/ext/xmlrpc/tests/bug40576_64bit.phpt
+++ b/ext/xmlrpc/tests/bug40576_64bit.phpt
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@ Bug #40576 (double values are truncated to 6 decimal digits when encoding)
 <?php
 if (!extension_loaded("xmlrpc")) print "skip";
 if (PHP_INT_SIZE != 8) die("skip this test is for 64bit platform only");
+if (strpos(xmlrpc_encode(1.123456789), "1.123456789") === false) die("skip the system libxmlrpc-epi formats doubles with six decimal places");
 ?>
 --INI--
 precision=12
